<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <!--
        The register, written the way a Baghdad diwan writes it.

        Four things in here are worth looking at rather than reading past.

        **Two numbers, never one.** ``our_number`` is our number in our book;
        ``their_number`` and ``their_date`` are theirs, copied exactly as they
        wrote them. Every attempt to normalise the second into the first loses
        the string the ministry will quote back down the telephone.

        **The chase is not the submission.** Three تذكير entries sit against the
        same submission. They are the kind that is repeatable and that does not
        restart the clock, so the file shows one submission with three chases -
        not four submissions.

        **The return is not a rejection.** The Commission sent the return back to
        have two supporting schedules completed. Recorded as إعادة للاستكمال it
        increments the round; recorded as a rejection it would poison every
        statistic the department is judged on.

        **The telephone consumes no number.** The last entry against the tax file
        is a contact note: no register, no ``our_number``, a named human, what he
        said, and a promised date. It moves the reply clock and suppresses the
        next chase, which is the difference between software that knows the
        section head has already answered and software that keeps writing to a
        man who told us to come back after the tenth.

        And one incoming letter has **no case at all** - an assessment for 2024
        that arrived unasked. That nullable link is why the mail room can be the
        landing screen.
    -->
